### Start a Zot registry

#### Basic usage

The image includes a default configuration that listens on port 5000 and stores data at `/var/db/zot`. Start a Zot registry with:

```console
$ appjail oci run -Pd \
    -o overwrite=force \
    -o virtualnet=":<random> default" \
    -o nat \
    ghcr.io/appjail-makejails/zot zot
```

Verify the registry is running:

```console
$ curl -i http://zot:5000/v2/
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Authorization,content-type,X-ZOT-API-CLIENT
Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,OPTIONS
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
Content-Type: application/json
Docker-Distribution-Api-Version: registry/2.0
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 04:44:10 GMT
Content-Length: 0

```

#### With persistent storage

For production use, mount a volume to persist registry data:

```console
$ mkdir -p /var/appjail-volumes/zot/data
$ appjail oci run -Pd \
    -o overwrite=force \
    -o virtualnet=":<random> default" \
    -o nat \
    -o fstab="/var/appjail-volumes/zot/data /var/db/zot" \
    ghcr.io/appjail-makejails/zot zot
```

#### With custom configuration

Mount your own Zot configuration file to `/usr/local/etc/zot/config.json`:

```console
$ mkdir -p /var/appjail-volumes/zot/data
$ appjail oci run -Pd \
    -o overwrite=force \
    -o virtualnet=":<random> default" \
    -o nat \
    -o fstab="/var/appjail-volumes/zot/data /var/db/zot" \
    -o fstab="/path/to/config.json /usr/local/etc/zot/config.json nullfs ro" \
    ghcr.io/appjail-makejails/zot zot
```

#### AppJail Director

```yaml
options:
  - virtualnet: ':<random> default'
  - nat:

services:
  zot:
    name: zot
    makejail: gh+AppJail-makejails/zot
    options:
      - expose: '5000:5000'
    volumes:
      - data: /var/db/zot
      - config: /usr/local/etc/zot/config.json

volumes:
  data:
    device: /var/appjail-volumes/zot/data
  config:
    device: ./config.json
    options: ro
```

### Default configuration

The image ships with a minimal configuration:

```json
{
    "storage": {
        "rootDirectory": "/var/db/zot"
    },
    "http": {
        "address": "0.0.0.0",
        "port": "5000",
        "compat": ["docker2s2"]
    },
    "log": {
        "level": "debug"
    }
}
```

* `compat: ["docker2s2"]` enables Docker registry v2 compatibility for Docker CLI push/pull.
* The registry listens on all interfaces (`0.0.0.0`) on port `5000`.
* No authentication is configured by default. Add access control settings for production.

### Web UI

The UI is only served when the search and ui extensions are enabled in your configuration:

```json
{
    "storage": {
        "rootDirectory": "/var/db/zot"
    },
    "http": {
        "address": "0.0.0.0",
        "port": "5000",
        "compat": ["docker2s2"]
    },
    "log": {
        "level": "info"
    },
    "extensions" : {
        "search": { "enable" : true },
        "ui": { "enable" : true }
    }
}
```

Start the ui with that configuration:

```console
$ appjail oci run -Pd \
    -o overwrite=force \
    -o virtualnet=":<random> default" \
    -o nat \
    -o fstab="/path/to/config.json /usr/local/etc/zot/config.json nullfs ro" \
    ghcr.io/appjail-makejails/zot zot
```

The UI is served at the server root. Open `http://zot:5000/` in a browser.
